    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0618" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg538"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Russell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 605.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to herewith forward copies
                    with translations of a letter from the provisional president of the State of
                    Barcelona to Mr. Balz in regard to the latter’s arrest some months ago, and of
                    Mr. Balz’s reply to General Rodriguez. Mr. Balz has not communicated with me as
                    yet. This correspondence was sent to our consul in La Guaira. I await your
                    further instructions in this matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William W.
                    Russell.</hi></signed></closer>



